jawt: return "no AWT" for any headless-only build, not just embedded

libjawt fails to link once the build is genuinely headless:

  ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: awt_GetDrawingSurface
  >>> referenced by jawt.o:(JAWT_GetAWT)

The makefile already anticipates this: with BUILD_HEADLESS_ONLY it links
libjawt against -lawt_headless and compiles it with -DHEADLESS. jawt.c has the
matching branch -- JAWT_GetAWT returning JNI_FALSE, commented "there are no AWT
libs available at all" -- but gates it on JAVASE_EMBEDDED as well, so a
headless build outside the embedded profile falls through to the code that
wires up the X11 drawing-surface entry points.

Those symbols live in libawt_xawt, which a headless-only build never produces,
so the branch applies whenever HEADLESS is defined. Widening the guard leaves
the embedded case exactly as it was and fixes every other headless build.

diff --git a/jdk/src/solaris/native/sun/awt/jawt.c b/jdk/src/solaris/native/sun/awt/jawt.c
index 64284bc..5d37e3d 100644
--- a/jdk/src/solaris/native/sun/awt/jawt.c
+++ b/jdk/src/solaris/native/sun/awt/jawt.c
@@ -33,7 +33,8 @@
  */
 JNIEXPORT jboolean JNICALL JAWT_GetAWT(JNIEnv* env, JAWT* awt)
 {
-#if defined(JAVASE_EMBEDDED) && defined(HEADLESS)
+/* A headless-only build has no libawt_xawt at all, embedded profile or not. */
+#if defined(HEADLESS)
     /* there are no AWT libs available at all */
     return JNI_FALSE;
 #else
